    "https://www.angelo.edu/career/": {
      "title": "Center for Career and Professional Success",
      "description": "Center for Career and Professional Success  · Angelo State University Skip to Main content Angelo State University Search Toggle Search Form Apply Toggle Main Menu Give Center for Career and Professional Success Angelo State is committed to helping students and alumni launch successful careers. Academics Academic Programs Departments Colleges Courses Academic Advising Academic Calendar About ASU History Core Values News Traditions About San Angelo Welcome from the President Mission Statement Admissions & Aid Apply to ASU Admitted Students Request More Information Visit Angelo State University Paying for College Life on Campus Live Play Lead Work Explore Community ASU Mayer Museum Alumni Association Small Business Development Center West Texas Collection Natural History Collections Kay Bailey Hutchison Institute Laura W. Bush Institute for Women’s Health Arts at ASU Planetarium Stephens Chapel Ranch and Meat Market ASU Ticket Office Summer Camps and Conferences Give to ASU Make a Gift Signature Events Join Athletics Quick Links RamPort Library Bookstore Events Public Health Updates Administration Research Mental Health Services Title IX/Incident Report En Español Information For Current Students Faculty & Staff Admitted Students Military Parents & Families Alumni Visitors School Counselors Online Students In this section Center for Career and Professional Success Handshake Internships and Experiential Learning Student Internships and Experiential Learning International Student Resources On-Campus Jobs Résumés Cover Letter Job Search Interviewing Tips Employer Resources and Opportunities Career Fair Preparation Career Exploration Choosing a Major Four-Year Plan What can I do with this major? Work Abroad Military and Veterans Office Policies Contact the Center for Career and Professional Success Home / Center for Career and Professional Success Our mission is to provide quality services and programs to guide ASU students and graduates through all stages of the career decision-making process, as well as to teach the job search skills they will utilize throughout life. From Campus to Career: Support Every Step of the Way Handshake Handshake is ASU’s official career platform. Use it to explore opportunities, post openings and apply for positions that match your goals. Internships Learn how to build practical experience that develops your skills and positions you for career success. Presentation Requests Invite our team to present on career topics for your class, student organization or group. Appointments Book a one-on-one appointment for tailored career support, from résumés and mock interviews to coaching and networking with alumni. Book an Appointment Upcoming Career Events More Events Sept. 22 REAL Rams: Headshots and Handshake , Sept. 22, 10:30 a.m. - 12:30 p.m., Rassman Building, Room 100 10:30 a.m. - 12:30 p.m. Rassman Building, Room 100 Sept. 24 CPT Pathways for International Rams , Sept. 24, 10  - 11 a.m., Houston Harte University Center, UC 201 10 - 11 a.m. Houston Harte University Center, UC 201 Sept. 29 REAL Rams: Résumé Ready (Engineering) , Sept. 29, 1  - 3 p.m., Vincent Building, Room 254 1 - 3 p.m. Vincent Building, Room 254 Career Exploration Discover your strengths, explore majors and career paths , and build a plan for your future. From résumé tips and job search strategies to career assessments and graduate school guidance, we offer tools and support to help you take the next step with confidence. Ram Network Stay connected with inspiring stories from the Ram Family—featuring alumni achievements, career tips and event highlights, all in one place. Discover More Alumni Spotlight: Kaci Foote Griffin , Mar 16 Animal Science, 2009 | Graduate Degree, 2011 Intern Spotlight: CJ Pena , Dec 5 Class of 2025, Bachelor of Business Administration (B.B.A.) in Management Alumni Spotlight: Kyle Suratt , Nov 18 Class of 2012, Bachelor of Arts (B.A.) in Mass Media Coursera Career Academy Develop new skills and earn microcredentials to enhance your degree. All courses are free for Angelo State students, alumni, faculty and staff. Learn More About Coursera The Ram Guide Blog: Career Tips for Your Future The Ram Guide From exploring career options and internships to mastering résumés, interviews and networking, The Ram Guide Blog offers practical advice to help you prepare for what’s next and launch your career with confidence. Charging Forward: Turning Your Degree into a Career You’ll Love Level Up Your Résumé: How College Internships Give You an Edge What Is a Graduate Degree? Find Out If It’s the Right Next Step for You We’re Here to Help! Center for Career and Professional Success 325-942-2255 career@angelo.edu Map: Houston Harte University Center , 107 ASU Station #11026, San Angelo, TX 76909 Quick Links Employers On-Campus Jobs Military & Veterans Office Policies If you want to go fast, go alone. But if you want to go far, go together. Go as a Ram. Apply Visit Us Request Info 2601 W. Avenue N San Angelo, TX 76909 1-800-946-8627 Campus Map Contact ASU University Directory RamPort Jobs at ASU Facebook X Instagram YouTube ©2026 Angelo State University All Rights Reserved Editor Login Scroll to Top TTU System Texas Tech University TTU Health Sciences Center TTUHSC El Paso Midwestern State University Institutional Résumés ASU Privacy Policy Weather and Emergency Notifications Mental Health Services Title IX/Incident Report State of Texas Statewide Search Texas Homeland Security Texas Veterans Portal State Auditor’s Office Fraud Prevention Site Policies"
    },
    "https://employment.angelo.edu": {
      "title": "Angelo State University Employment Site",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Home Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Angelo State University has been named a “Great College to Work For” every year since 2015. Guided by our core values of Integrity, Diversity and Inclusion, Significance, Community, and Commitment, ASU fosters a collaborative environment where employees thrive and make a difference. Explore opportunities below and become part of a university dedicated to excellence and student success. Faculty Positions Staff Positions Student Positions Adjunct About Angelo State University Benefits at a Glance Contact Us If you have questions, please call the Office of Human Resources at (325) 942-2168 \r\nor email hr@angelo.edu . Clery Act Statement Angelo State University complies with the Jeanne Clery Act, which requires universities \r\nto publish an Annual Security Report (ASR) containing campus crime statistics, safety \r\npolicies, and procedures. ASU's ASR is available online, and printed copies may be \r\nrequested from the University Police Department . EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
