brary Resources for Faculty Research Disability Services Dual Credit Instructors Registration and Advising Academic Advising Academic Calendar Class Schedule Course & Instructor Information Degree Programs DegreeWorks Navigate360 Registrar’s Office Registration and Scheduling University Catalogs Students in Need When our students need help, we’re here to help them however we can. The following resources can be a life-line to a student in need. ASU Cares Counseling Services Crisis Help Line Emergency Aid and Loans Emergency Alert Sign-up Incident Report Ram Pantry Title IX University Police University Clinic Contact Information Administrative Support Offices Campus Directory Colleges Departments Employee Banner Login Faculty Senate Human Resources Parking President’s Academy for Life-Long Leaders Staff Senate Administration and Accreditation Academic Assessment IDEA Finance Budget Office Contracts and Materials Management Contracting Office Controller’s Office Purchasing Fraud Prevention Travel Resources Technology Information Technology Technology Knowledge Portal Computer Labs & Services Technology Service Center Work Order IT Policies & Procedures IT Privacy Policy IT Support Services Request Form for New Employee Webmail (O365) Technology Project Request Emergency ASUAlert Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Emergency Management Environmental Health, Safety and Risk Management Police Blotter University Police 2601 W. Avenue N San Angelo, TX 76909 1-800-946-8627 Campus Map Contact ASU University Directory RamPort Jobs at ASU Facebook X Instagram YouTube ©2026 Angelo State University All Rights Reserved Editor Login Scroll to Top TTU System Texas Tech University TTU Health Sciences Center TTUHSC El Paso Midwestern State University Institutional Résumés ASU Privacy Policy Weather and Emergency Notifications Mental Health Services Title IX/Incident Report State of Texas Statewide Search Texas Homeland Security Texas Veterans Portal State Auditor’s Office Fraud Prevention Site Policies"
    },
    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8143": {
      "title": "Angelo State University Employment Site",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Admissions Counselor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Admissions Counselor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Admissions Counselor Position Number 998123; 997878, 977620 Department Admissions Salary $40,000 Remote No Job Summary Dedicated to student recruitment and enrollment success, the Admissions Counselor serves as a primary liaison between Angelo State University and prospective students, families, educators, and community partners. Responsible for managing an assigned territory, the role coordinates recruitment initiatives, represents the university at on- and off-campus events, and guides students through the admissions process. Success in this position requires strong relationship-building skills, a commitment to exceptional service, and the ability to communicate the academic and student life opportunities that make Angelo State University an institution of choice. Essential Duties Lead a successful territory recruitment plan by: providing exceptional customer service to prospective students, their families, and key partners at high schools and community colleges; analyzing application and enrollment trends to inform recruitment strategies; adjusting outreach efforts based on data and feedback; communicating with students and families in a timely and professional manner; represent Angelo State University – traveling to recruitment events and delivering presentations to prospective and admitted students, parents, and other target populations Support prospective students by: staying well-versed in admissions standards, placement tests, and academic requirements; serving as a knowledgeable resource on FAFSA deadlines and processes; possessing a broad understanding of university programs and services to make appropriate referrals; communicating effectively with different audiences; ensuring students are informed of deadlines, procedures, and eligibility criteria Take a proactive approach to student engagement by using our Customer Relationship Management ( CRM ) system to: identify and connect with prospective students using various communication methods (text, email, phone, virtual meetings); keep outreach efforts organized by logging interactions promptly and accurately; guide outreach strategies to high schools and community colleges Build and maintain relationships with high school and community college partners by: sharing timely, relevant information that supports students through every stage of their journey; staying informed about academic calendars for target area and how they impact outreach; identifying Angelo State University key services for prospective and current students and connecting students to the appropriate department when necessary; sharing relevant updates with internal and external stakeholders to enhance the student experience Play an active role in creating a welcoming and high-performing team environment within the Office of Admissions by: supporting campus visit programs through presentations, guided campus tours, carrying out assigned duties during recruitment events, and conducting after tour meetings; responding to inquiries via phone, email, and text with professionalism and care in a timely manner; participating in meetings, committees, and special projects as needed; assisting with training and professional development of fellow team members; collaborating on team initiatives, assisting team members as needed (specifically during busy travel season), and performing other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge: Undergraduate admissions policies, procedures, eligibility requirements, and enrollment practices. University academic programs, student services, campus resources, and student life opportunities. Financial aid processes, including FAFSA requirements, deadlines, and supporting documentation. Customer relationship management ( CRM ) systems, such as Salesforce, and data-informed recruitment strategies. Skills : Building relationships and providing exceptional customer service. Verbal and written communication, including presentations and public speaking. Organization, time management, and multitasking in a fast-paced environment. Analyzing recruitment data, identifying trends, and recommending solutions. Using Salesforce, Microsoft Office Suite, and virtual communication platforms. Planning, coordinating, and executing recruitment and outreach events. Abilities : Build and maintain positive relationships with prospective students, families, school counselors, and community partners. Work independently, exercise sound judgment, and make effective decisions. Manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and adapt to changing demands in a fast-paced environment. Collaborate effectively with colleagues and stakeholders across the university. Maintain confidentiality, professionalism, and a student-centered approach to service. Travel and work evenings and weekends as needed to support recruitment activities. Minimum Qualifications Education: A Bachelor’s degree is required Valid driver’s license Travel for several weeks in the fall and in the spring and some evenings and weekends Preferred Qualifications Fluent in Spanish. Master’s degree in student counseling, education, business or Public Relations, or other related field. Knowledge of Texas and Angelo State University. Experience working in an admissions office, operating audio/visual/video equipment, and computer experience. Extensive experience in recruiting, public relations, sales, marketing, or related fields. Ability to learn admissions and financial aid requirements and deadlines for high school and transfer students; general knowledge about all Angelo State University programs, majors, services, their requirements, restrictions and costs. Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1164P Open Date 09/02/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 10/01/2026 Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/7545": {
      "title": "HVAC Technician I",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | HVAC Technician I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices HVAC Technician I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title HVAC Technician I Position Number 999048 & 999512 Department Facilities Management Salary $38,500 Remote No Job Summary Under general supervision, performs skilled mechanical work in the operation, maintenance, and repair of the university’s HVAC and Central Plant systems. Works under the direction of the Lead HVAC /Controls Technician to carry out both corrective and preventive maintenance tasks, ensuring efficient and reliable system performance. Essential Duties Lubricates and cleans mechanical parts, as well as changes air filters on equipment Participates in repair and maintenance of HVAC , refrigeration and related mechanical equipment with difficult or special problems. Performs water test, analyzes and treats hot, chilled and condenser water systems. Maintains equipment logs. Keeps Lead HVAC /Controls Technician informed of equipment status, communicates with Facilities Management personnel, faculty, staff and contractors and attends trainings, seminars, and other meetings as needed. Performs after hour, holiday and weekend repairs on a rotating on call schedule and as needed in the event of emergencies. Performs other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of the principles and practices of HVAC systems maintenance, including related electrical and pneumatic controls. Basic knowledge of math, algebra and geometry. Good communication skills, both written and verbal. Ability to gain knowledge of university policies and procedures. Knowledge of environmental requirements related to building maintenance. Demonstrate initiative and perform quality work in a busy, multi-task environment. Basic knowledge of chemistry and physics as related to plant issues. Ability to operate computer keyboard. Ability to troubleshoot equipment to component level. Ability to read and understand complex manuals and diagrams. Must be able to adjust to changing priorities. Ability to operate maintenance vehicles, industrial hand and power tools, welder, personnel lifts, fork lift, computers, sheet metal fabrication, equipment, software, fax, copier, and calculators. Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or GED certification required. 3 years HVAC experience Technician type I or higher. Refrigeration EFA approved certification is required. Technical school training in HVAC or related systems preferred. Must have a valid Texas driver’s license and have a driving record acceptable to the University’s insurance company. Preferred Qualifications Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1013P Open Date 07/22/2025 Close Date Desired Start Date 08/18/2025 Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume List of References Optional Documents Cover Letter Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8054": {
      "title": "Angelo State University Employment Site",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Head Coach - Shotgun Sports Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Head Coach - Shotgun Sports Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Head Coach - Shotgun Sports Position Number 977373 Department Student Affairs Salary $50,000 - $60,000 Remote No Job Summary Shotgun Sports Head Coach (co-curricular competitive club sport) is responsible for organizing and overseeing team practices, recruiting new students, managing team events and enhancing the overall competitiveness and success of the team. Essential Duties Coaching: Organize and oversee a standardized and regimented practice schedule for the team. Identify points of development for all team members in all disciplines. Develop plans and techniques to improve skills and competition results. Create curricula for mental development to improve focus, confidence, and success in practice and competition environments. Recruiting: Develop a recruiting schedule for Texas and other national events. Represent ASU and the Shotgun Sports program at events, providing information to potential students and parents. Adhere to established recruitment goals and quotas. Organize and highlight recruit signing events. Forecast student graduation rates and develop recruiting strategies to fill gaps created by graduation within the team dynamics. Team Management: Manage team budget and fundraising events. Plan and execute team events and competitions. Procure team equipment, including vests, ammunition, and other necessary items. Handle registration, travel plans, accommodations, and team meals for competitions. Maintain communication with parents, donors, and home club relations. Advising: Conduct new member orientation and classroom tours prior to the start of the semester. Review grades and academic progress of each competitor each semester. Aid in guidance and support of academic obligations of team members throughout the academic year. Fundraising: Develop and maintain sponsor relationships. Grow hosted benefit and competition events. Identify and leverage grant opportunities. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge Knowledge of shotgun sports rules, coaching principles, firearm safety practices, and range operations. Knowledge of NCAA , conference, university, and applicable state and federal regulations related to intercollegiate athletics and firearm use. Knowledge of program administration, including budgeting, scheduling, inventory management, and fundraising principles. Skills Strong organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills. Skill in recruiting, evaluating, and selecting qualified student-athletes. Skill in developing, implementing, and evaluating training programs and practice plans. Skill in instructing shotgun shooting techniques, firearm safety procedures, and range protocols. Abilities Ability to coach, supervise, mentor, and motivate student-athletes while supporting their academic and athletic success. Ability to safely operate, handle, and oversee the use of shotguns and related shooting equipment. Ability to exercise sound judgment and respond effectively to safety concerns and emergency situations. Ability to build and maintain effective working relationships with student-athletes, recruits, staff, alumni, donors, and the public. Minimum Qualifications Competitive experience in NSCA , NSSA , or ATA , or a combination of any governing body listed. High School Diploma Preferred Qualifications Proven coaching and team organizational experience preferred Bachelor’s degree preferred Valid instructor certification from NSCA , NSSA or ATA preferred Recruiting success experience preferred Fundraising experience and event management experience preferred. Physical Requirements Ability to stand and walk for extended periods while coaching, supervising practices, and attending competitions. Ability to lift, carry, push, and pull equipment, ammunition, targets, and supplies weighing up to 50 pounds. Ability to bend, stoop, kneel, reach, and perform repetitive motions associated with coaching activities, equipment setup, and range management. Ability to maintain visual acuity sufficient to monitor shooting performance, range conditions, and safety compliance at varying distances. Ability to work outdoors in varying weather conditions, including heat, cold, wind, dust, and precipitation. Ability to travel, including overnight travel, for competitions, recruiting activities, and other program-related functions. EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1165P Open Date 08/26/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 10/01/2025 Review Start Date 09/16/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required 