    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/7811": {
      "title": "Angelo State University Employment Site",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Adjunct (Cybersecurity) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Adjunct (Cybersecurity) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct (Cybersecurity) Position Number 00000 Department Computer Science Salary Commensurate Remote Job Summary The Department of Computer Science at Angelo State University seeks qualified applicants for Adjunct Instructor positions in Cybersecurity beginning Fall 2026. The department offers Bachelor of Science degrees in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, and Artificial Intelligence, as well as Master of Science degree programs in Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence. Essential Duties Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in Cybersecurity in both online and face-to-face formats. Develop and deliver instructional materials and assess student learning outcomes. Support a dynamic and engaging learning environment for students. Provide high-quality educational experiences in Cybersecurity for both majors and non-majors. Maintain regular communication with students and uphold academic standards. Collaborate with faculty to support and enhance curriculum development, ensuring alignment with industry standards. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge Knowledge of cybersecurity concepts and practices sufficient to support instruction at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Knowledge of effective teaching methodologies and student-centered learning approaches. Skills Strong instructional and teaching skills. Skill in delivering course content in both online and face-to-face formats. Skill in developing engaging and innovative learning environments. Skill in integrating technology to enhance student learning. Strong organizational and time management skills. Abilities Ability to create a supportive learning environment that promotes student success. Ability to communicate effectively with students and colleagues. Ability to collaborate in a team-oriented environment. Ability to manage workload, adapt to changing needs, and contribute to a dynamic academic setting. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Computer Science or a closely related field. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching courses in computer science or cybersecurity at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Experience in cybersecurity course or curriculum development. Experience with graduate instruction, advising, or relevant professional or scholarly activity. Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number F162P Open Date 06/15/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 08/17/2026 Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed ASU Employment Website Texas Workforce Commission Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Transcripts (Unofficial) List of References Optional Documents Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
