    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/7909": {
      "title": "Department Chair (Computer Science)",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Department Chair (Computer Science) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Department Chair (Computer Science) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Department Chair (Computer Science) Position Number 999263 Department Computer Science Salary Commensurate Remote No Job Summary The Chair of the Department of Computer Science at Angelo State University provides academic, administrative, and strategic leadership for a dynamic department committed to excellence in teaching, student success, curriculum innovation, and faculty collaboration. Reporting to the Dean of the College of Science and Engineering, the Chair is responsible for fostering a student-centered culture that promotes retention, graduation, and career readiness while ensuring a high-quality, cohesive curriculum across undergraduate and graduate programs. The Chair will lead efforts to strengthen academic programs through continuous assessment and improvement, support faculty development and scholarly activity, promote a collaborative and inclusive departmental culture, and build partnerships that enhance student learning and workforce preparation. The successful candidate will provide visionary yet practical leadership that balances innovation with operational excellence and advances the mission of the department, the college, and Angelo State University. Essential Duties Student Success Provide leadership to improve student success through effective advising, student engagement, retention initiatives, timely graduation, and career preparation. Foster a student-centered culture that promotes academic achievement and prepares graduates for successful careers and advanced study. Curriculum Leadership Lead the continuous review, assessment, and improvement of undergraduate and graduate curricula to ensure academic quality, appropriate course sequencing, industry relevance, and alignment with student learning outcomes. Promote collaboration among faculty to maintain a cohesive and high-quality educational experience across all programs. Faculty Leadership and Department Culture Recruit, mentor, evaluate, and support faculty while fostering a collaborative, collegial, and accountable departmental culture. Encourage excellence in teaching, scholarship, service, and shared governance, while promoting open communication and teamwork across the department. Research and External Partnerships Support faculty and student scholarship, external funding opportunities, and interdisciplinary collaboration. Develop partnerships with industry, government, alumni, and community organizations that enhance student learning, workforce development, and the department’s regional impact. Operational Leadership Provide effective administrative leadership by overseeing course scheduling, workload assignments, budgeting, personnel, facilities, and other departmental operations. Ensure compliance with university policies while promoting efficient and transparent decision-making. Assessment and Continuous Improvement Promote a culture of continuous assessment and evidence-based decision making. Use program assessment, student success data, and faculty input to strengthen academic programs, improve operational effectiveness, and support continuous departmental improvement. Strategic Leadership Develop and implement a strategic vision that strengthens the department’s academic foundation while positioning it for sustainable growth. Work collaboratively with the dean, faculty, students, and external stakeholders to advance the mission of the department, the College of Science and Engineering, and Angelo State University. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge Knowledge of academic leadership and operations within a computer science department, including curriculum development, student success initiatives, faculty evaluation, assessment, budgeting, and university policies and procedures. Knowledge of effective teaching practices, student learning, curriculum design, and continuous program improvement, including the use of assessment data to support evidence-based decision making. Knowledge of faculty development, shared governance, accreditation, strategic planning, and best practices for leading a collaborative academic department. Skills Strong interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills, with the ability to build trust, foster collaboration, and work effectively with faculty, staff, students, alumni, and external partners. Demonstrated leadership and consensus-building skills with the ability to facilitate productive discussions, resolve conflicts, and guide departments through organizational change. Skill in strategic planning, project management, and organizational leadership, with the ability to balance long-term vision and day-to-day operational effectiveness. Skill in developing partnerships with industry, government, alumni, and community organizations that enhance student learning, experiential education, workforce development, and external funding opportunities. Abilities Ability to provide visionary and collaborative leadership that promotes student success, academic excellence, faculty engagement, and a positive departmental culture. Ability to lead continuous improvement through curriculum review, assessment, strategic planning, and the effective use of institutional data. Ability to recruit, mentor, evaluate, and support faculty while fostering accountability, professional growth, and shared governance. Ability to manage departmental operations effectively, including budgeting, personnel, scheduling, and resource allocation, while ensuring compliance with university policies. Ability to support excellence in teaching, scholarship, service, and community engagement while advancing the mission of the department, the college, and Angelo State University. Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution, with academic credentials sufficient to teach and provide leadership across undergraduate and graduate computer science programs. Eligibility for appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor in the Department of Computer Science at Angelo State University. Demonstrated record of excellence in teaching, scholarly achievement, and service appropriate for appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. Demonstrated academic leadership experience, such as department chair, associate chair, program director, assistant dean, dean, or other significant academic leadership experience in higher education. Demonstrated experience leading curriculum development, program assessment, faculty development, student success initiatives, or other continuous improvement efforts in higher education. Preferred Qualifications Experience serving as a department chair or in a comparable academic leadership role. Experience leading accreditation, assessment, or continuous improvement initiatives. Demonstrated success improving student success, retention, graduation, or career readiness. Experience recruiting, mentoring, evaluating, and developing faculty. Demonstrated ability to build a collaborative and collegial departmental culture. Experience developing partnerships with industry, government, alumni, or community organizations. Demonstrated success obtaining external funding, grants, or industry support for academic programs or research. Physical Requirements No physical requirements. EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number F379P Open Date 07/20/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 06/01/2027 Review Start Date 10/02/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
