    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/7524": {
      "title": "Angelo State University Employment Site",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Adjunct of Bassoon and Oboe Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Adjunct of Bassoon and Oboe Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Provide links to recordings of 3 recent solo performances (last 4 years). Recordings should be submitted via Dropbox, Google, YouTube links, etc. Official transcripts will be required of the finalists. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct of Bassoon and Oboe Position Number 999468 Department Visual and Performing Arts Salary Doctorate-$3,230 per course; Masters-$2,584 per course Remote No Job Summary The Music Area of the Department of Visual and Performing Arts at Angelo State University seeks to fill the position of Adjunct Double Reed Instructor for the 2024-25 academic year. This position calls for an individual with a commitment to undergraduate Music Education who will teach applied double reeds (bassoon and oboe). Essential Duties Teach applied lessons in oboe and bassoon, a weekly studio class, reed making, and chamber ensembles as assigned. In the Spring semester the teaching load includes the double reed section of a Woodwind Methods class. Additional courses may be assigned based upon experience and the needs of the music area. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Qualified candidates must possess strong communication and organizational skills, exhibit skill in musicianship, rehearsal techniques, and effectiveness as a teacher of university level music students, successfully recruit and retain students, work collaboratively and collegially within a university environment, and meet the needs of a diverse student body. Minimum Qualifications Masters Degree in Music with focus in Oboe or Bassoon. Proven record of teaching both oboe and bassoon students. Experience teaching reed making for both oboe and bassoon. Experience in teaching Woodwind Methods. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate or ABD (with doctorate conferred at time of appointment) in music, with focus in Oboe or Bassoon. Experience in teaching Woodwind Methods. Experience teaching reed making for both oboe and bassoon. Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number F284P Open Date 07/01/2024 Close Date Desired Start Date 08/26/2024 Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Provide links to recordings of 3 recent solo performances (last 4 years). Recordings should be submitted via Dropbox, Google, YouTube links, etc. Official transcripts will be required of the finalists. Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Other Optional Documents List of References 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8131": {
      "title": "Angelo State University Employment Site",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Police Officer II Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Police Officer II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. 1st Shift 6:45AM-2:45PM 2nd Shift 2:45PM-10:45PM Power Shift 7PM-3AM 3rd Shift 10:45PM-6:45AM Available for recall as needed for campus emergencies. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Police Officer II Position Number 999494 Department University Police Salary $48,000 - $50,000 Remote No Job Summary Under general supervision, performs law enforcement and public safety duties to protect life and property on campus. Enforces university policies and regulations, as well as applicable local, state, and federal laws, while providing services that support a safe and secure environment for the Angelo State University community. Essential Duties Patrols campus areas on foot or in patrol vehicle to control traffic, prevent crime or disturbances, and enforce applicable rules and laws. Responds to a variety of calls for police services. Investigates accidents, incidents, crimes, and prepares investigative offense reports. Assists in maintaining a safe campus by responding to fire and burglar alarms; medical emergencies and ensuring the physical security of campus buildings. Issues citations for traffic and parking violations on campus and adjacent city streets. Provides security and crowd control services at University-sponsored events and functions, as assigned; transports money to and from various campus locations as requested. Arranges for abandoned or impounded vehicles to be towed away. Provides customer service to students, faculty, staff and university visitors by providing directions and other assistance as needed. Escorts injured persons to medical facilities, as deemed appropriate. Documents and reports any threats to public safety. Testifies in court or at hearings on accident, theft, burglary, and other cases; serves subpoenas. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of the principles, practices, and procedures of law enforcement and public safety; Knowledge of applicable rules, regulations, policies, and procedures utilized in campus law enforcement and security; Knowledge of the use and maintenance of firearms; knowledge of campus buildings and facilities and their uses. Ability to interpret and appropriately apply applicable rules, regulations, policies, and procedures; Ability to communicate effectively with students, faculty, staff, visitors, and others contacted in the course of work; Ability to effectively analyze situations, use good judgment, and take appropriate action; Ability to follow written and verbal instructions and complete work as assigned; Ability to work various shifts, as assigned. Skilled in interpersonal communications and relations; Skilled in the use of a firearms and other non lethal weapons; Skilled in self-defense tactics. The University Police Department will furnish approved duty weapon. Candidate is required to pass a physical performance evaluation ( WORKSTEPS ) performed by the West Texas Rehab Center. Ability to successfully pass an entry level written and grammar evaluation. Ability to successfully pass a psychological and background assessment. Ability to complete other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Successfully graduated high school or possess equivalent GED . Possess a Basic Texas Peace Officer License from the Texas Commission on Law Enforcement ( TCOLE ) plus one year experience in law enforcement or related field. Preferred Qualifications Physical Requirements Candidate is required to pass a physical performance evaluation ( WORKSTEPS ) performed by the West Texas Rehab Center; including drug testing. EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1175P Open Date 09/18/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 10/01/2026 Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants 1st Shift 6:45AM-2:45PM 2nd Shift 2:45PM-10:45PM Power Shift 7PM-3AM 3rd Shift 10:45PM-6:45AM Available for recall as needed for campus emergencies. Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents List of References Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/7955": {
      "title": "Angelo State University Employment Site",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Mobile STEM CDL Driver (Part-Time) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Mobile STEM CDL Driver (Part-Time) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Mobile STEM CDL Driver (Part-Time) Position Number 977237 Department College of Science & Engineering Salary $24,700 Remote No Job Summary Angelo State University is seeking a CDL Driver for our STEM Innovation Lab. The ASU STEM Innovation Lab is a high-tech mobile platform bringing immersive science, technology, engineering, and math ( STEM ) experiences directly to rural and underserved communities across West Texas. Essential Duties Safely operates university-owned, leased, or rented buses and passenger vehicles in accordance with applicable federal and state laws and university policies. Transports authorized passengers to local and distant destinations according to approved schedules and itineraries. Conducts and documents required pre-trip and post-trip inspections, including inspections of tires, lights, brakes, emergency equipment, fluid levels, safety systems, and the general condition of the vehicle. Completes driver logs, mileage records, inspection reports, fuel records, passenger documentation, and other required travel records accurately and promptly. Ensures that passengers follow applicable safety requirements and that vehicle capacity and safety limitations are not exceeded. Maintains passenger comfort systems, including climate controls and interior lighting, as applicable. Safely loads and unloads passengers and assists passengers with boarding and exiting when appropriate. Secures the vehicle whenever it is unattended and checks the passenger compartment at the conclusion of each trip. Immediately reports mechanical concerns, unsafe conditions, delays, traffic citations, collisions, injuries, and other incidents to the appropriate university representative. Follows university procedures for accidents, emergencies, roadside breakdowns, severe weather, and other unexpected events. Maintains professional conduct and provides courteous service when interacting with students, employees, minors, guests, and members of the public. Complies with all applicable U.S. Department of Transportation, Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration, Texas Department of Public Safety, Texas Department of Transportation, TTU System, and Angelo State University requirements. Participates in required university driver training, safety training, drug and alcohol testing, medical certification, and driver-approval processes. Performs other related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of safe commercial vehicle and passenger transportation practices. Knowledge of applicable traffic laws, commercial driver requirements, passenger-carrier safety requirements, and vehicle inspection procedures. Ability to safely operate the class and type of vehicle assigned by the university. Ability to complete pre-trip and post-trip inspections and recognize conditions that may make a vehicle unsafe to operate. Ability to read and follow maps, electronic navigation systems, schedules, itineraries, and written instructions. Ability to maintain accurate driving, inspection, mileage, fuel, and travel records. Ability to respond appropriately to emergencies, vehicle malfunctions, adverse road conditions, and schedule changes. Ability to communicate effectively and professionally with passengers, university employees, law enforcement personnel, emergency responders, and members of the public. Ability to work independently while maintaining communication with the supervising department. Ability to work irregular schedules, including nights, weekends, holidays, early mornings, overnight trips, and extended travel. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise appropriate judgment when transporting students, minors, employees, or other university participants. Ability to comply with ASU driver approval, insurance, safety, and risk-management requirements. Ability to perform the essential functions of the position with or without reasonable accommodation. Ability to sit for extended periods while operating a vehicle. Ability to safely enter and exit buses multiple times during shifts. Ability to lift and carry up to 50 pounds on an occasional basis. Ability to work outdoors in varied weather conditions. Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. At least 20 years of age. At least two years of licensed driving experience. Current and valid Commercial Driver License ( CDL ) of the class required for the vehicle being operated. Must not have a license restriction that prevents operation of the assigned university vehicle. Must possess and maintain any medical certification required for the assigned commercial driving duties. Must meet Angelo State University driver-approval requirements and receive approval from the university’s insurance carrier and Office of Environmental Health, Safety and Risk Management before operating a university vehicle. Must have an acceptable motor vehicle record. Must successfully complete all required criminal history, driving record, employment, and other applicable background checks. Must satisfy all applicable U.S. Department of Transportation and FMCSA drug and alcohol testing requirements, including pre-employment testing. Must authorize and successfully complete the required FMCSA Drug and Alcohol Clearinghouse query before performing safety-sensitive CDL duties. Must remain eligible under applicable CDL , DOT , FMCSA , Texas DPS , TTU System, and university requirements throughout employment. Must be able and willing to work irregular hours and travel locally or overnight as required. Strong communication and customer service skills. ASU currently requires all employees who operate university-owned, leased, or rented vehicles to complete its driver-approval process. ASU also states that drivers operating vehicles holding more than 15 passengers must possess a valid Texas CDL with the appropriate endorsements. (Angelo State University ) Federal guidance similarly requires a CDL with a passenger endorsement for vehicles designed to transport 16 or more people, including the driver. ( FMCSA ) Preferred Qualifications Previous bus driving experience in higher education, public transit, school transportation, charter service, or commercial transportation. Current Department of Transportation ( DOT ) medical certification. Experience transporting large groups and operating motor coaches or commercial passenger buses. Knowledge of vehicle inspection procedures and defensive driving practices. Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1151P Open Date 07/27/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
