    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8135": {
      "title": "Director of Instructional Design",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Director of Instructional Design Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Director of Instructional Design Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Director of Instructional Design Position Number 998501 Department Angelo State Global Salary $85,000 Remote No Job Summary The Director of Instructional Design provides leadership for online course development, instructional design services, faculty support, and digital learning innovation across Angelo State Global and the university. The position supervises instructional design staff, establishes quality standards for online learning, oversees course development initiatives, and collaborates with academic leaders to enhance teaching and learning. The Director is responsible for reimagining and advancing instructional design services to support enrollment growth, student success, faculty development, and the evolving needs of Angelo State Global and Angelo State University. Essential Duties Instructional Design Leadership- Provide leadership and supervision for instructional design staff and establish priorities, workflows, and service models that support online program growth and instructional excellence. Online Course Quality and Innovation- Develop and implement standards, processes, and continuous improvement practices that support high-quality online and hybrid learning experiences. Faculty Development and Support- Lead faculty development initiatives related to online teaching, course design, instructional technology, and emerging educational practices. Strategic Planning and Transformation- Develop and implement a future-focused vision for instructional design services that supports Angelo State Global, academic innovation, workforce-aligned programming, and institutional priorities. Collaboration and Institutional Partnerships- Collaborate with academic colleges, Academic Affairs, Information Technology, student support units, and university leadership to advance teaching and learning initiatives. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of instructional design principles, learning theory, and online pedagogy. Knowledge of online course quality standards and best practices. Knowledge of accessibility requirements and instructional technology tools. Knowledge of higher education course development processes. Knowledge of faculty development and instructional innovation strategies. Skilled in project management and team leadership. Skilled in supporting and consulting with faculty on course design and online teaching. Skilled in evaluating instructional technologies and emerging educational trends. Ability to lead and develop professional instructional design staff. Ability to build collaborative relationships across academic units. Ability to use data and assessment results to improve teaching and learning outcomes. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree from an accredited institution and five years of progressively responsible experience in instructional design, online learning, educational technology, faculty development, or a related field, including experience leading projects, initiatives, or professional staff. Preferred Qualifications Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1173P Open Date 09/10/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 10/15/2026 Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts (Unofficial) List of References Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/7542": {
      "title": "Angelo State University Employment Site",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Athletics Bus Driver (Part-time) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Athletics Bus Driver (Part-time) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. If you are currently a TRS contributing employee, then you will be required to contribute to TRS in this position. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Athletics Bus Driver (Part-time) Position Number 00000 Department Athletics Salary Commensurate Remote Job Summary Under the supervision of and reporting to the Director of Athletics, the employee is primarily focused on operating those vehicles used to transport passengers over specified routes to local or distant points according to a time schedule. Essential Duties Inspects the vehicle prior to each use to ensure proper and safe operation. Regulates heating, cooling, and lighting systems for passengers. Transports passengers over specified routes to local or distant points according to a time schedule (which often includes overnight trips, and extended trips requiring irregular hours. Complies with all applicable traffic regulations and reports all delays and accidents in an appropriate manner. Secures the vehicle when passengers/teams have disembarked for safety and security precautions. Reports any necessary repairs to the Director of Athletics or his designee. Conforms to and complies with all applicable federal and state transportation guidelines and requirements. Complete a pre and post trip inspection of the vehicle, and driver’s travel log. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Individuals must possess these required knowledge, skills and abilities to explain and demonstrate that he/she can perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation, using some other combination of skills and abilities. Ability to operate within all guidelines of Angelo State University and the Department of Athletics. Current CDL license category appropriate to driving university owned and/or rented passenger vehicles. Approval from university’s auto insurance carrier. Effective oral and written communication skills at a level sufficient to represent Angelo State University and the department of Athletics, and to perform the essential functions of the position. Ability to work, cooperate and maintain a professional rapport with all coaches, athletes, faculty and supervisory staff. Ability to work and travel at various hours, including nights and weekends, when required. Knowledge of and ability to comply with all applicable responsibilities (e.g. driver and vehicular) set forth by the U.S. DOT and TxDOT agencies. Ability to safely deliver passengers within scheduled timeframes. Minimum Qualifications A current commercial drivers license that encompasses all necessary endorsements to operate owned or rented vehicles is required. Additional Considerations: The university must obtain approval (via driving record checks) from its auto insurance carrier and risk management office for any driver employed by the department of Athletics. Must be willing to submit to background checks, including criminal history background checks, and non- CDL / DOT drug testing. All applicable CDL / DOT tests, etc. also apply. To be considered for this position, all candidates must sign appropriate releases permitting respective checks and/or testing. Preferred Qualifications Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number S450P Open Date 08/23/2021 Close Date Desired Start Date Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants If you are currently a TRS contributing employee, then you will be required to contribute to TRS in this position. Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8052": {
      "title": "Facilities Contract Coordinator",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Facilities Contract Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Facilities Contract Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Facilities Contract Coordinator Position Number 999769 Department Facilities Management Salary $41,250 Remote No Job Summary The Facilities Contract Coordinator supports the administration and coordination of contracted facilities services, custodial operations, and construction projects. This position serves as a central point of coordination between university departments, Facilities Management personnel, contractors, and vendors to support effective service delivery, contract administration, project execution, and fiscal accountability. The role helps ensure contracted services and projects align with institutional standards, operational needs, and budgetary requirements while promoting a safe, functional, and well-maintained campus environment. Essential Duties Monitors and manages project and service contract budgets to ensure expenditures remain within approved funding and encumbered purchase orders. Tracks financial activity, reconciles project balances, reviews invoices and pay applications, identifies discrepancies, and supports fiscal compliance across multiple contracts and projects. Creates purchase requisitions and prepares supporting procurement documentation for service contracts, construction projects, contract amendments, and other departmental needs. Ensures compliance with university procurement policies, state regulations, and contract requirements. Conducts custodial quality assurance inspections and contract compliance reviews to evaluate service delivery, cleanliness standards, and adherence to contract specifications. Documents deficiencies, tracks corrective actions, and monitors contractor performance to ensure continuous service improvement. Maintains and administers contract and project documentation, including inspection reports, service records, change orders, schedules, contract amendments, financial records, and other supporting documentation required for operational and audit purposes. Serves as a liaison between university departments, facilities personnel, contractors, vendors, and project managers to coordinate services, communicate expectations, address operational concerns, and facilitate timely resolution of issues related to custodial operations and construction projects. Provides administrative and operational support to Facilities Management leadership by preparing reports, maintaining performance metrics, assisting with audits, supporting project administration activities, and contributing to the effective management of contracted facilities services. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of custodial operations, quality assurance practices, contract compliance, and facilities services, including industry cleaning standards, inspection processes, and generally accepted maintenance practices. Knowledge of project and contract administration, including budget tracking, purchase requisition processing, invoice review, recordkeeping, and audit support. Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills with the ability to manage multiple projects, contracts, deadlines, and priorities while maintaining a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Ability to conduct inspections, evaluate service performance, identify deficiencies, and document findings, while supporting corrective action efforts and continuous improvement initiatives. Skilled in verbal, written, and interpersonal communication, with the ability to effectively work with university personnel, contractors, vendors, customers, and project stakeholders. Proficiency in Microsoft Office and other business software applications, with the ability to learn and utilize financial, procurement, work management, and contract management systems. Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or GED . Two (2) years of experience in facilities management, contract administration, project administration, construction administration, custodial operations, or a related field. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Valid Texas driver’s license and a driving record acceptable to the University’s insurance carrier. Must successfully pass a background check. Preferred Qualifications Associate’s or Bachelor’s degree in Business, Accounting, Facilities Management, Construction Management, or a related field. Experience performing inspections, quality assurance reviews, contract monitoring, or vendor performance evaluations. Knowledge of custodial industry standards, APPA cleanliness standards, or commercial cleaning operations. Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1162P Open Date 08/25/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 09/16/2026 Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
