    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8100": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of English",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Assistant Professor of English Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Assistant Professor of English Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants for the position should submit a cover letter, CV, transcripts, and three letters of recommendation. Review of applications will begin immediately. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor of English Position Number 998687 Department English & Modern Languages Salary $53,500 Remote No Job Summary The Angelo State University Natalie Zan Ryan Department of English and Modern Languages is seeking a tenure-track Assistant Professor of English, specializing either in pre-Civil War American literature or post-World War II American literature. The position also includes teaching core curriculum courses in writing and literature, advanced undergraduate courses, and graduate courses for the online English MA program. The successful candidate will be broadly trained in American literature beyond their research specialization. Essential Duties The dedicated educator and scholar will teach a range of courses across the English curriculum, including: First-Year Composition Sophomore-level American Literature Upper-division undergraduate English courses Online graduate-level English courses The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. Responsibilities include: Engaging in scholarly research and publishing in the candidate’s area of specialization Advising and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students Participating actively in departmental, university, and community service Contributing to curriculum development and program enhancement Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge English composition and American literature. Current trends, research, and scholarship in English studies and the candidate’s area of specialization. Skills Teaching first-year composition and literature courses. Instructional design and curriculum development for undergraduate and graduate courses, including online delivery. Written and verbal communication. Organization, time management, and prioritization. Abilities Design and deliver engaging instruction across undergraduate and graduate levels, including online formats. Mentor and advise students effectively. Collaborate professionally with colleagues and participate in academic governance. Contribute to departmental, university, and community service initiatives. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in English or a closely related field ( ABD considered with expected completion by start date) Evidence of effective teaching at the college level A record of or potential for scholarly publication Preferred Qualifications Experience with online instruction is preferred Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number F383P Open Date 09/08/2026 Close Date 12/15/2026 Desired Start Date 08/23/2027 Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants for the position should submit a cover letter, CV, transcripts, and three letters of recommendation. Review of applications will begin immediately. Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts (Unofficial) List of References Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
