    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8122": {
      "title": "Angelo State University Employment Site",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Enterprise Systems Analyst I-III Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Enterprise Systems Analyst I-III Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Enterprise Systems Analyst I-III Position Number 998588 Department Information Technology Salary $60,000 - $70,000 Remote No Job Summary Under the guidance of the Information Technology leadership team, the Enterprise Systems Analyst will focus on designing, developing and improving the University’s processes and services through the support, augmentation, and development of technology software applications. Provides integration and support for applications, programs and scripts to simplify the customer experience. Develops processes and applications for data and authentication integration. Facilitates and/or leads discussions with technical peers, vendors, and leadership teams to anticipate/resolve problems and develop solutions for campus needs to ensure high availability. This technical support position requires resolving complex technical challenges in the Banner Student environments, including platform customization and customer-facing app creation using both code-based and no-code tools. Collaboration is key, with responsibilities including effective communication across teams and vendors, partnering with users to generate insightful reports, and supporting peers and student technicians. Additionally, the role contributes to strategic technology evaluations and stays current with emerging tools to enhance university-wide systems and services. Essential Duties Application Development & System Integration: Assists in the design, development and support for university applications and their integration into other technical and functional areas. Assists in working with functional users, create reports and support business needs for day-to-day operations and identify trends to improve business processes. Efficiently and creatively solve moderately difficult or complex problems that affect immediate work team and/or extended team. Serve as a key contributor in group troubleshooting and resolution. Data Management and Platform Support: Assists in managing data operations including imports, exports, and cleansing to ensure data integrity and accuracy. Contributes knowledge in resolving complex challenges in Salesforce development, including platform customization, system integration, and customer-facing app development using both code-based and no-code tools. Supports automation and synchronization of new and existing university systems and services. Collaboration and Operational Reporting: Communicates effectively with functional teams, technical staff, and vendor partners to manage expectations and foster collaboration. Partners with functional users to support daily operations and identify trends to improve business processes. Coordinates closely with project leads on customer-specific initiatives involving data translation or integration support and development. Technical Problem Solving and Strategic Planning: Assists in creative problem-solving to moderately complex challenges, supports peers and student technicians, and plays a key role in collaborative troubleshooting. Assists to university-wide technology evaluations, offering strategic recommendations to improve processes and productivity, while staying informed about emerging tools and coordinating closely on data integration initiatives. Utilizes ticketing and project management tools to manage requests, incidents, changes, and projects while ensuring timely updates and resolution. Collaborates with the Information Security Team to enforce security standards and partners with IT staff and campus officials to support disaster recovery and business continuity efforts. Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of: Banner and related software that would facilitate improved business processes. Power BI & Cognos reporting toolset. SQL programming language as it relates to a database environment. Applicable University rules, regulation, policies, and procedures. Principles, practices, and procedures of computer programming/scripting. Database environments. PHP , Python, SQL , PL/ SQL . Systems Development Life Cycle ( SDLC ). Data reporting, dashboards, and outcome tracking for program assessment. Skill in: Best-practice programming/scripting techniques. Secure coding practices. Adapting and maintaining existing applications, frameworks, and API’s. Interpersonal relations and project management. Expressing technical terminology in an understandable manner to customers. Ability to: Communicate effectively with customers and others contacted in the course of work. Effectively analyze situations and develop suitable solutions. Work under pressure in a fast-paced environment and adapt to change in procedures and priorities. Research new technology items and to learn new technologies. Collaborate effectively with IT, academic departments, and external partners. Solve problems independently, make informed decisions, and manage confidential information. Work evenings or weekends when project deadlines or events require. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, M.I.S. or related field required. Additional experience in the support of a networked desktop/application environment may substitute for the Bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. Minimum of two (2) years of technology-related experience required. Additional consideration may be given to candidates with specific technical certifications related to systems applicable to Angelo State University. Job title of Enterprise Systems Analyst I- III along with salary will depend on the applicant’s qualifications. Preferred Qualifications Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1148P Open Date 07/17/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 11/02/2026 Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other * This position requires full-time, on-site work in San Angelo, Texas and is not eligible for remote or hybrid work arrangements. Are you able and willing to meet this requirement? Yes No * Why did you choose ASU? (Open Ended Question) * Please describe the attributes that will make you a strong candidate for this position (Open Ended Question) * In less than five sentences, please describe the ideal work environment. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * What's your favorite programming language and why? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
