    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/7901": {
      "title": "Assistant Women's Soccer Coach",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Assistant Women&#39;s Soccer Coach Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Assistant Women's Soccer Coach Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Women's Soccer Coach Position Number 999479 Department Athletics Salary Commensurate Remote No Job Summary Assists the Head Women’s Soccer Coach with the administration and daily operation of the NCAA Division II Women’s Soccer program. Supports all aspects of the program, including coaching, recruiting, student-athlete development, compliance, game and event operations, and community engagement. Promotes a positive student-athlete experience that encourages academic achievement, competitive success, leadership development, and sportsmanship while representing Angelo State University in a professional manner. Essential Duties Supports the administration and daily operation of the Women’s Soccer program and ensures compliance with all NCAA , Lone Star Conference, Angelo State University, and Texas Tech University System policies, rules, and regulations. Assists the Head Coach in planning and conducting practices, training sessions, and competitive activities while providing instruction in soccer fundamentals, techniques, strategies, and conditioning. Assists in the identification, evaluation, and recruitment of prospective student-athletes who demonstrate the academic and athletic potential to contribute to the program. Supports student-athlete success by encouraging academic achievement, personal development, leadership, and overall well-being. Provides guidance and support to graduate assistant coaches, student assistants, managers, and student-athletes while assisting with program administration, game-day operations, event management, and team travel. Supports the visibility and success of the Women’s Soccer program through community engagement, public relations activities, camps, clinics, fundraising initiatives, and other outreach efforts. Represents Angelo State University, the Athletics Department, and the Women’s Soccer program in a professional and positive manner with students, alumni, supporters, and the community. Performs other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of soccer fundamentals, techniques, strategies, rules, and conditioning principles. Knowledge of NCAA , conference, and University rules, regulations, and policies. Ability to instruct, motivate, and develop student-athletes. Ability to identify, evaluate, and recruit prospective student-athletes. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with students, coaches, staff, and community stakeholders. Strong organizational, interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and work a flexible schedule, including evenings, weekends, and travel. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from a regionally accredited college or university. Soccer coaching experience and/or collegiate playing experience. Demonstrated knowledge of soccer fundamentals, techniques, strategies, and player development. Ability to work evenings, weekends, and travel as required. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree from a regionally accredited college or university. Intercollegiate soccer coaching experience, preferably at the NCAA level. Experience recruiting prospective student-athletes. Experience working in a collegiate athletics environment. Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1145P Open Date 07/17/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 08/10/2026 Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Transcripts (Unofficial) 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
