    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8130": {
      "title": "Angelo State University Employment Site",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Plumber I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Plumber I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Plumber I Position Number 998828 Department Facilities Management Salary $39,000 Remote No Job Summary Under general supervision, performs plumbing and related work of moderate difficulty. May work independently and assist others. Essential Duties Studies building plans and working drawings to determine supplies and tools required, and sequence of installations; plans and organizes work to ensure completion of tasks and functions in an efficient and timely manner. Locates and marks position of pipe connections and passage holes for pipes in walls and floors, using tape measure, spirit level, and plumb bob; cuts openings in walls and floors , using hand tools and power tools. Installs, repairs, and maintains water, gas, air, sewer lines and systems according to specifications and plumbing codes. Connects and maintains hot water units, water heaters, garbage disposal units, dishwashers, and water softeners. Installs and maintains a variety of controls, including mixing valves, temperature control valves, PRV’s and related. Installs and repairs a variety of pumps and related systems. Opens clogged drains and toilets. Repairs and maintains valves, faucets, traps, sinks, washbowls, vents, and toilet fixtures. Joins pipe by using screws, bolts, fittings, solder, plastic solvent, PEX , and Pro Press piping. Cuts and threads pipe, using pipe cutters, cutting torch, and pipe threading machine; bends pipe to required angle by using pipe bending machine or bending by hand. Fills pipe system with water or air and reads pressure gauges to determine if system is leaking. Notifies management concerning the need for major repair projects; prepares supply requirement lists and forwards to supervisor. Attends training, seminars, and other meetings as needed. Performs after hour, holiday and weekend repairs on a rotating on call schedule and as needed in the event of emergencies. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Ability to interpret and work from building plans, rough sketches and drawings. Ability to plan and lay out installation and/or repair projects. Ability to follow written and verbal instructions and complete work as assigned. Ability to understand and utilize installation and maintenance manuals, procedures and other related materials. Skilled in the use of the standard tools, equipment, and machines of the plumbing trade. Equipment Utilized: Maintenance vehicle, backhoe, trencher, hand tools, soldering tools, tape measure, power tools, pipe cutters, threading machines, PEX , Pro Press and pressure gauges. Minimum Qualifications Completion of high school, vocational school, or any combination of experience and training which provides the knowledge, skills and abilities for successful performance in the position. Five years of plumbing experience. State of Texas Journeyman plumber’s license Must have a valid Texas driver’s license and have a driving record acceptable to the University’s insurance company. Must pass a pre-employment physical and criminal background check. Preferred Qualifications Physical Requirements Position requires frequent walking, standing, reaching, bending, and occasional crawling, climbing and lifting (up to 80 lbs.). Basic manual dexterity with both hands is required. Incumbent works both indoors and out doors and is exposed to dust, heat, cold, and varying climatic conditions. EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1177P Open Date 09/18/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 10/02/2026 Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume List of References Optional Documents Cover Letter 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
