    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8134": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Art, Video Game Art and Animation",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Art, Video Game Art and Animation Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Assistant Professor of Art, Video Game Art and Animation Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants interested in being considered for an interview should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, statement describing their research and/or creative practice, contact information for three professional references, and examples of professional and student work. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor of Art, Video Game Art and Animation Position Number 977225 Department Visual and Performing Arts Salary $53,500 Remote No Job Summary The Angelo State University College of Arts and Humanities and Department of Visual and Performing Arts invites applications from qualified candidates to teach online and face-to-face courses in Video Game Art and Animation. The Bachelor of Fine Arts in Video Game Art and Animation is a new degree within the Department of Visual and Performing Arts. The ideal candidate will be able to help shape this degree for the next generation of video game artists. Applications will be accepted continuously and reviewed as instructional needs develop. Ideal candidates will demonstrate strong abilities in art, creativity, design, and technology, supported by professional or academic experience in game design, technical art, real-time production, and game development processes. They should be capable of integrating visual arts with technology and teaching students how visual design, 3D modeling and asset creation, animation, lighting, materials, shaders, optimization, and interactive features function together in professional game-production settings. They will also mentor students with backgrounds in graphic design, digital art, and traditional fine arts. The goal is to help students transfer their existing artistic knowledge into game development and build industry-focused technical art portfolios that demonstrate professional-level skills. Essential Duties Teaching: Instruct undergraduate studio art courses ranging from foundation drawing and design to courses involving Real-Time, Level Dressing, VFX for games, 2D Animation, 3D Modeling and Sculpting, Lighting, Rendering and Look Development. Other art courses as assigned. Research and Creative Works: Maintain a significant, ongoing studio practice with a record of professional accomplishments, such as solo and group exhibitions at local, regional, national or international levels. Professional Service: Serve on departmental and university committees. Manage studio facilities and assist in the coordination of the Video Game Art and Animation program. Participate in student recruitment and retention. Participate in departmental and Art Area meetings and events. Maintain regular office hours. Work collaboratively and productively with faculty colleagues to meet the needs of the student body. Curriculum Development: Lead or collaborate on revisions of the curriculum, integrating traditional skills with conceptual and interdisciplinary practices. Create curriculum for new courses within the VGAA curriculum to include both online and face-to-face modalities. Mentorship: Academic advising and mentoring BFA art students. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Proficiency in 2D and 3D digital art tools used in contemporary game and animation production. Proficiency in 3D asset creation and integration, procedural production techniques, lighting, materials, shaders, rigging, animation systems, artist-oriented scripting, AI-supported creative workflows, XR optimization, and other commonly used tools and processes associated with game development and real-time production. Ability to recruit, retain students in the Video Game Art and Animation concentration. Participate in departmental/Art Area meetings and events. Maintain regular office hours. Work collaboratively and productively with faculty colleagues to meet the needs of students and the Art Program. Minimum Qualifications An MFA or PhD in game design, game programming, or a closely related discipline, including fields such as computer science, computer programming, or interactive design. Preferred Qualifications Professional experience within the game industry is highly desirable. At least two years of hands-on experience in game development using Unreal Engine production methods. Strong technical proficiency with Unreal Engine, Microsoft Visual Studio, C++, C#, Python, JavaScript, HLSL / GLSL , Verse, Advanced Blueprint Visual Scripting, computer graphics math, performance profiling, and specialized pipelines like Niagara VFX , animation and rendering. Familiarity with industry-standard software, tools, and production workflows, including Autodesk Maya, Mudbox, Adobe Substance 3D, Adobe Creative Cloud, Blender, and ZBrush. Physical Requirements Standing/sitting, bending, lifting, carrying as necessary per the job duties. EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number F388P Open Date 09/18/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 01/19/2027 Review Start Date 10/19/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants interested in being considered for an interview should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, statement describing their research and/or creative practice, contact information for three professional references, and examples of professional and student work. Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Transcripts (Unofficial) List of References Other Optional Documents 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/7541": {
      "title": "Angelo State University Employment Site",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Athletics Event Staff (Part-time) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Athletics Event Staff (Part-time) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Athletics Event Staff (Part-time) Position Number 000000 Department Athletics Salary Commensurate Remote Job Summary Athletics Event Staff members will be needed for Angelo State University home athletic events (football, volleyball, soccer, softball, baseball, basketball, track & field). Essential Duties Duties vary with positions that are available and needed for athletic events. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Must be capable of working collegially with a diverse group of faculty, staff and students on a daily basis. Excellent customer service skills and ability to interact with the public is required. Minimum Qualifications Must be dependable and able to work flexible hours, mostly evenings and weekends. Must be willing to become a part of the “team ASU ” culture as well as exhibiting great customer service skills. Preferred Qualifications Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number S470P Open Date 10/12/2021 Close Date Desired Start Date Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8038": {
      "title": "Accountability Data Specialist",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Accountability Data Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Accountability Data Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Accountability Data Specialist Position Number 999827 Department Office of Accountability Salary $71,000 - $74,672 Remote No Job Summary Designs and develops dataset preparation, reporting, and decision support solutions. Captures requirements and designs, creates, manages, and fulfills requests for Accountability/institutional compliance needs, Accountability federal reporting requirements, campus reports, dashboards, and scorecards through report writing tools, including SAS , Microsoft Power BI, IBM Cognos, and other software tools. Works in the Office of Accountability and collaborates with Information Technology on data access and architecture needs to ensure information is accessed and managed in a common way. Supports reporting requirements for IPEDS , THECB , LBB , and other accountability initiatives. Essential Duties Plans and organizes work to ensure completion of tasks and functions in a timely manner, prior to all deadlines. Prepare data visualizations of university data (strategic dashboards, scorecards, and complex reports) based on goals, priorities and key performance indicators. This includes using SAS and other reporting/data visualization tools (example: Microsoft Power BI, IBM Cognos and other software) for reporting needs. Propose/initiate procedures and evaluate existing procedures to effect improved or additional methods for handling or reporting information. Focus on compliance and information reports for the campus and governing bodies like SACSCOC , the Texas Tech University System, Texas Higher Education Coordinating Board, IPEDS , etc. Strong general programming skills to provide data needed to support institutional decision-making. Provide strategic information analysis and decision support by identifying gaps and outliers in data as projects are being created, updated, or analyzed. Proactively identify data issues, propose solutions, and respond to requests to address data quality and analysis concerns. Work with Accountability leadership to develop and implement protocols, processes, and timelines for data collection, data review and correction, and dataset preparation. Manage access/protocols to the Accountability reporting environment to ensure that key stakeholders have appropriate/need-to-know access to data. Ensure access to sensitive information is adequately protected and only given to individuals with appropriate approvals, including an institutional justification with a ‘need to know’ approach. Coordinate with Information Technology to ensure access methods align with campus requirements. Leverage multiple database resources appropriately to ensure consistent data management methods are followed. Work closely with Information Technology to collaborate and align data management procedures ensuring data is used in a manner consistent with its meaning and following agreed-upon campus reporting naming conventions and processes when creating and managing reports/dashboards. Address reporting issues as they arise and help to maintain Accountability infrastructure. Maintains consistent and accurate communication with the Assistant Vice President of Accountability and Analytics as well as constituencies. Assists the Assistant Vice President of Accountability and Analytics in monitoring changes, in a timely manner, and adhering to institutional, state, and/or federal rules and regulations. Prepares correspondence and other written documentation ensuring timelines and milestones are met. Participates in training activities and meetings as required or needed. Performs other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge Experience of SAS software and reporting tools such as (Microsoft Power BI, IBM Cognos, and other associated components). Knowledge of design, development, and maintenance of Business Intelligence reports, dashboards, metrics, and other reporting constructs. Knowledge of the Analytics/Report Design processes, strategic thinking, critical thinking, analytical ability. Knowledge of relational database, SAS , SQL and query tools. Skills Skill in priority and time management. Skill in SQL and structured programming techniques. Skill in maintaining accurate records and logs Abilities Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and written, with skill in interpersonal relations. Ability to interpret and understand the needs and concerns of collaborators to generate appropriate follow-up analyses, reports, and identification of potential planning priorities. Ability to effectively analyze situations and develop suitable solutions. Ability to work as a cooperative team member across all levels of the organization, while also having strong independent skills. Ability to share knowledge while also keeping confidentiality and secure PII and other protected data and information. Ability to work with large and complex computer databases. Ability and willingness to pay attention to detail, organize, be proactive, think logically, work both independently and in groups, work with numbers, maintain confidentiality and follow policies and regulations. Ability to perform mathematical calculations Ability to organize workflow and complete detailed tasks accurately and in a timely manner Ability to maintain confidentiality and follow policies and regulations Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a quantitative field, computer science, MIS , business, or another related field. Three years of experience using reporting software such as SAS and other reporting tools (example: Microsoft Power BI, IBM Cognos, etc) or area dealing with numbers—and accompanying issues regarding accuracy, organization, and detail—and record of supporting multiple but very different projects simultaneously using programming. Preferred experience and qualifications can stand in lieu of education. Must be willing to work additional hours during peak times and/or flexible schedule to accommodate business needs. Preferred Qualifications The following is not required; however is preferred. Knowledge and/or experience with data extraction tools SAS Enterprise guide, SQL , interactive analytic or dashboard of SAS , Microsoft tools, Tableau, data extraction tools. Physical Requirements Requires prolonged period of sitting, occasional walking, and intermittent bendingand standing; medium level of manual dexterity; occasional lifting up to 25-50 lbs. EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number S1161P Open Date 08/20/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 09/08/2026 Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other * Familiarity with Excel? I am an Excel Expert (Can Create Pivot Tables, formulas) I am an Excel Accomplished (Can maneuver excel, formulas, and create multi-sheet links) I am an Excel Novice (can only sort) * I am comfortable training and creating trainings? I have created and trained large groups of people (10+). I have created training but not trained. I have trained but not created the training. I have created and trained small groups of people (<10). * Do you have knowledge and/or experience with computer programs or languages. If so, which programs or languages (Open Ended Question) * Do you have experience with SAS Enterprise Guide? I am a SAS Expert. I am SAS Accomplished (Can manuever and create)/ I am familiar with SAS. I have not used SAS; however am willing to learn. * Will you require sponsorship to work in the US now or in the future? YES NO * This position requires full-time, on-site work in San Angelo, Texas and is not eligible for remote or hybrid work arrangements. Are you able and willing to meet this requirement? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Transcripts (Unofficial) Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/7512": {
      "title": "Angelo State University Employment Site",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Adjunct (Mass Media) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Adjunct (Mass Media) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct (Mass Media) Position Number 999467 Department Communication and Mass Media Salary Master’s: $2,584 / class PhD: $3,230 / class Remote Job Summary ASU Department of Communication and Mass Media is developing a pool of potential adjuncts. Any position available through this posting is a temporary appointment to teach courses in the specified department, which also determines the number and types of courses. This posting is intended to generate a pool of qualified individuals who may be eligible for the different types of positions that may come open in the department. The successful applicant will possess strong mass media and communication skills with an ability and desire to teach mass media courses in the department curriculum such as writing for mass media, news reporting and writing, media literacy, media management, and others. Essential Duties Candidates should be dedicated to excellence in teaching, prepare syllabi and course materials, deliver lectures, grade and assign grades. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Candidates should be dedicated to excellence in teaching. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in journalism, mass media or mass communication. Preferred Qualifications Prior college-level teaching experience and 18 hours in advanced journalism, mass media, or mass communication. Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number F196P Open Date 03/24/2022 Close Date Desired Start Date Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts (Unofficial) List of References Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Other Resume 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
